Z||000000||Voyd||10-31-1999||03:55 PM||||whats the diffrence a V6 '85 SE and GT?<P>reason i ask is becuase i bought an SE according to the VIN decoder,but there is a GT front fascia on it, and GT emblems on the front and on the steering wheel. it has power everything and sunroof. <P>id just like to know what a GT would have that my car doesnt have right now. <P>thanks||||reg||5
Z||000001||Raydar||11-01-1999||09:29 PM||||The V-6 85 SE was equipped with all of the GT running gear, suspension and options. The GT added the Indy Pace Car bodywork. AFAIK, the wing was only available on the GT. This was the only "notchback" GT. In 86 they became fastbacks, and the SE adopted the notchback and Indy bodywork.<p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 11-01-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Raydar||11-01-1999||09:31 PM||||The 85 SE was equipped with all of the GT running gear, suspension and options. The GT added the Indy Pace Car bodywork. AFAIK, the wing was only available on the GT. This was the only "notchback" GT. In 86 they became fastbacks, and the SE adopted the notchback and Indy bodywork.||||reg||1
